    "pageType": "text",
    "text": "CHAPTER 6\nChapter 6: The Weekly System. Proof\nIt's Working.\nYou've got your numbers, your tracker, your steps, and your program. This chapter is the control\ntower: the simple weekly routine that proves the plan is working and tells you exactly what to\nadjust when it isn't. Ten minutes a week. No guessing, ever again.\nRule 1: Weigh Every Morning, Trust Only the Weekly Average\nEvery morning: wake up, bathroom, then scale, before any food or water. Same scale, same spot\non the floor. Log the number next to your calories and steps.\nNow the part that saves your sanity: a single day's weight means nothing. Your weight swings\n2 to 5 pounds day to day from water, salt, carbs, and what's sitting in your gut. None of that\nswing is fat. People quit great programs every week because Tuesday's number jumped from a\nsalty dinner.\nSo we never judge a day. Every 7 days, add up the week's weigh ins, divide by 7, and compare\nthat average to last week's average. The average filters out the water noise and shows you the\nfat truth.\nRule 2: Know What the Average Should Do\nGo back to your Chapter 2 worksheet. Your daily deficit ÷ 500 = your predicted loss per week in\npounds. A 500 deficit predicts about 1 pound a week. A 1,000 deficit predicts about 2. Compare\nyour weekly averages against that prediction.\nWeek 1 warning: your first week will probably show a BIG drop, sometimes 3 to 6 pounds. Enjoy\nit, and know that most of it is water and gut content clearing out as you eat less. That's normal.\nIt's also why week 2 can look slow. The real fat rate reveals itself from week 2 onward.\nRule 3: The Stall Protocol\nHere's the entire adjustment system:\nIf your weekly average dropped: it's working. Change nothing. Keep going.\nIf your weekly average stalled for ONE week: do nothing yet. One flat week happens, usually\nwater hiding a real fat loss. Stay the course.",
