    "text": "CHAPTER 7\nChapter 7: The Guarantee. In Writing.\nI'm not asking you to believe me. I'm asking you to follow the program with a camera in your\nhand and let the scale settle it. Here's my end of the deal.\nThe Promise\nFollow this program for 90 days. If you don't lose at least 10 pounds, I'll pay you back\nDOUBLE what you paid for this book.\nI can make this offer loudly for one reason: the program's proof requirements and its success\nrequirements are the same actions. If you do the things that make you eligible, the 10 pounds\ncome off. The guarantee isn't a safety net under the program. It IS the program.\nWhat \"Following the Program\" Means\nTo be eligible for the 2X guarantee, all six of these, for all 90 days:\n1. Register your start. Within 7 days of purchase, send your Day 1 email to\nksiguineau@gmail.com with: your completed Chapter 2 worksheet, a photo of your morning\nweigh in (feet and scale reading visible), and your chosen daily calorie number. Your 90 days\nstart on the date of that email.\n2. Log every day of food. A daily calorie total in your tracker, all 90 days.\n3. Photograph everything you eat. Every meal, every snack, every drink that isn't water, before\nyou eat it. This is the backbone of the proof and the backbone of your results. They're the same\nthing.\n4. Weigh in every morning. Logged daily. Plus a scale photo on Day 1, Day 30, and Day 90.\n5. Hit your steps. 10,000 a day logged, from your phone or watch. Miss a day here and there?\nLife happens. Your 90 day average needs to sit at 10,000 or above.\n6. Do the workouts. Three sessions a week, logged (gym program from Chapter 5 or the\nbodyweight version). At least 33 total sessions across the 90 days.\nYour calorie target must follow Chapter 2's rules, including the intake floor. A deficit of at least\n500 calories a day is required to make the math capable of 10 pounds.\nHow to Claim",
